    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110471" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάω</span></b> 
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">[ᾰ</span>], <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>shine,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάε δὲ χρυσόθρονος Ἠώς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					14.502
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Χηλαὶ λεπτὰ φάουσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arat.
					607
				</span></i>
			:—<i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i> also cites a part.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῶντα</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάμποντα</span>
			, and 
				Ep.
			aor. 2
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πέφη</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐφάνη.</span>
			 (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φαϝ-,</span> cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φάος, φαῦσις.</span>)</div>
